## 2. Zero-Copy Remap Strategy

### Tensor Naming Incompatibility
  GLM-5.3-Flash:  model.language_model.layers.N.*  (75,760 tensors)
  Colibri expects: model.layers.N.*  (no language_model prefix)

### Approach: Header-Only Index Patch (NO weight duplication)
  1. Download model shards as-is (195 GB on NVMe)
  2. Patch model.safetensors.index.json — strip "model.language_model." prefix
  3. Physical shard files: NEVER TOUCHED (read-only by Colibri C-loader)
  4. Colibri loads tensor names from index, physical bytes from shards

### Script Created
  /home/sascha/halostream/spike/remap_glm53.py
  - Reads existing index (JSON)
  - Remaps keys: model.language_model.* → model.*
  - Writes patched index back (in-place)
  - Original backed up as model.safetensors.index.json.pre_remap

### Vision Encoder (model.visual.*)
  Kept as-is — Colibri Vulkan backend ignores vision tensors for text inference.
  Only text decoder layers are used.

### Remapped Key Categories
  model.language_model.*  →  model.*           (75,760 tensors)  ← REMAPPED
  model.visual.*          →  model.visual.*    (347 tensors)    ← KEPT AS-IS
  lm_head.weight          →  lm_head.weight   (1 tensor)       ← KEPT AS-IS

